{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"light probe reference for cg light probe reference for cg","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md","fileName":"Light Probe Reference for CG.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Light Probe Reference for CG","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CG Integration and Render Passes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","Plate Lighting Reference for CG","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"light probe reference for cg light probe reference for cg","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Light Probe Reference for CG.md","fileName":"Light Probe Reference for CG.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Light Probe Reference for CG","heading":"Light Probe Reference for CG","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An omnidirectional light probe records the incident illumination around a point, supplying both a record of a location and a possible image-based-lighting source. The book distinguishes a high-dynamic-range probe from an ordinary spherical lighting reference that captures similar directions without the same intensity range. Bracketed exposures can be merged to extend that range. Even a regular blurred environment image may provide useful soft fill, often combined with a separate sun or key light. The goal is a match to the photographed set, not merely a technically elaborate lighting rig. See [[Plate Lighting Reference for CG]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["